te": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 879121, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LAoqsyYkLQV7yDnTKxdMYc", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 885016, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and PR #101 against main is open with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** My request to open the PR timed out, so I checked the list of open PRs before trying again. PR #101 had been created, but with no reviewers attached, so I added alex to it instead of opening a second PR.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID. I relied on the docstring and the test, which agree with each other.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Q88DYHs6ruaCGMUbSKemme", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KzMYyxspYVUJrZcKFcHsxb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TrNat85LNvZYv7XFC8stY4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_rea