on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_017HZ7cSwZMNEWMfABC1uNK2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LAoqsyYkLQV7yDnTKxdMYc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and PR #101 against main is open with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** My request to open the PR timed out, so I checked the list of open PRs before trying again. PR #101 had been created, but with no reviewers attached, so I added alex to it instead of opening a second PR.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID. I relied on the docstring and the test, which agree with each other.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}